(257519, 16516, 6999, '<td valign="top">Of the three best phtos in this challenge, this was the lowest placed: you''re a victim of the symmetry obsessives, and thos wwho can''t be bothered to read the challenge instructions. never mind, it remains a fabulous photo. The others, by the way, placed 72nd and 101st - so your in pretty good company.<br/> <br/>Ed<br/> <br/>edit: obviously, by ''best'', I mean IMO.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-04-08 14:28:41.</i></td>', 'Of the three best phtos in this challenge, this was the lowest placed: you''re a victim of the symmetry obsessives, and thos wwho can''t be bothered to read the challenge instructions. never mind, it remains a fabulous photo. The others, by the way, placed 72nd and 101st - so your in pretty good company. Ed edit: obviously, by ''best'', I mean IMO.', '2003-04-07 19:33:08.000000', '2003-04-08 15:28:41.000000', 0),
(257527, 16300, 6999, '<td valign="top">One of my three favourites this week - the others placed 72nd and 109th. Good taste will always be in a minority. But let me just say again, this a fabulous photo.<br/> <br/>Ed</td>', 'One of my three favourites this week - the others placed 72nd and 109th. Good taste will always be in a minority. But let me just say again, this a fabulous photo. Ed', '2003-04-07 19:35:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(257530, 16413, 3607, '<td valign="top">i saw the symmetry but just didn''t find the picture very compelling (which is just a way of me saying i can''t tell you why i didn''t like it).  did you consider submitting it in b&amp;W?  i just took a look at it that way and thought that it captured your lighting much better, and it removes the distraction of the brown floor tiles by turning them into a complimentary dark/light pattern to the side.</td>', 'i saw the symmetry but just didn''t find the picture very compelling (which is just a way of me saying i can''t tell you why i didn''t like it).  did you consider submitting it in b&W?  i just took a look at it that way and thought that it captured your lighting much better, and it removes the distraction of the brown floor tiles by turning them into a complimentary dark/light pattern to the side.', '2003-04-07 19:35:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(257564, 16638, 1439, '<td valign="top">Damn! It should have score much higger</td>', 'Damn! It should have score much higger', '2003-04-07 19:50:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(257634, 16694, 327, '<td valign="top"><b>CC-Hello</b> Annida <br/> <br/>Fits The Challenge- Yes<br/>Composition- Confusing, my eye can''t find a place to land.<br/>My Opinion- Like many below I found this a bit too dark to make out what it is. I''m not sure yet and I did try to lighten it up. I think the brass or bright areas picked up all the light available. Sorry, don''t mean to totally stomp on your shot. I see your ISO was 200 &lt;?&gt; a night time shot? Okay ....chin up and get on the next challenge and start shooting.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-04-07 19:37:53.</i></td>', 'CC-Hello Annida  Fits The Challenge- YesComposition- Confusing, my eye can''t find a place to land.My Opinion- Like many below I found this a bit too dark to make out what it is. I''m not sure yet and I did try to lighten it up. I think the brass or bright areas picked up all the light available. Sorry, don''t mean to totally stomp on your shot. I see your ISO was 200 <?> a night time shot? Okay ....chin up and get on the next challenge and start shooting.', '2003-04-07 20:37:19.000000', '2003-04-07 20:37:53.000000', 0),
(257707, 16176, 3575, '<td valign="top">Gordon, this is gorgeous. It is so clear and sharp and colorful! I love the surface of the water. What an excellent enticement for tourism to Melbourne! I just can''t get over the colors. Amazing shot.</td>', 'Gordon, this is gorgeous. It is so clear and sharp and colorful! I love the surface of the water. What an excellent enticement for tourism to Melbourne! I just can''t get over the colors. Amazing shot.', '2003-04-07 21:02:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(257893, 16638, 1344, '<td valign="top">What the heck is Olympus 2 in 1 mode?</td>', 'What the heck is Olympus 2 in 1 mode?', '2003-04-07 22:52:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(257977, 16176, 2109, '<td valign="top">Can you make this available as a print?  Very well done ... absolutely amazing shot!</td>', 'Can you make this available as a print?  Very well done ... absolutely amazing shot!', '2003-04-07 23:32:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(258018, 16630, 4267, '<td valign="top">greatness.. how any of the scores are as low as they are is beyond me.. sheesh.. great work</td>', 'greatness.. how any of the scores are as low as they are is beyond me.. sheesh.. great work', '2003-04-07 23:50:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(258336, 16640, 6458, '<td valign="top">OeBi..<br/> <br/>"In PS I removed dust &amp; scratches and I lifted the contrast"  <br/> <br/>You do realize that removing dust and scratches violates the rules of the challenges? Unless you''re using some techinque that affects the entire picture, that''s considered spot editing. I appologize in advance if you removed them by some other means.<br/> <br/>-Matt</td>', 'OeBi.. "In PS I removed dust & scratches and I lifted the contrast"   You do realize that removing dust and scratches violates the rules of the challenges? Unless you''re using some techinque that affects the entire picture, that''s considered spot editing. I appologize in advance if you removed them by some other means. -Matt', '2003-04-08 05:15:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(258407, 16638, 6349, '<td valign="top">Hey.  I have the same camera as you and I don''t know about this 2 in 1 mode.  Please enlighten me.</td>', 'Hey.  I have the same camera as you and I don''t know about this 2 in 1 mode.  Please enlighten me.', '2003-04-08 07:23:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(258462, 16625, 5792, '<td valign="top">This was one of my top three choices for this challenge.<br/> <br/>The quality of this image plus the deliberate joke poking fun at the "symmetry" theme was hilarious and incredibly well done. It has just the right amount of a warped sense of humor.</td>', 'This was one of my top three choices for this challenge. The quality of this image plus the deliberate joke poking fun at the "symmetry" theme was hilarious and incredibly well done. It has just the right amount of a warped sense of humor.', '2003-04-08 08:57:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(258468, 16176, 5792, '<td valign="top">I gave this image one of the low scores.<br/> <br/>When trying to figure out why it got such a high rating I decided to looked at it again. This is a stunning night cityscape and a very deserving winner.<br/> <br/>My apologies to you. I must have be asleep at the clicker when this gem whooshed by. Can I change my vote now?  :)</td>', 'I gave this image one of the low scores. When trying to figure out why it got such a high rating I decided to looked at it again. This is a stunning night cityscape and a very deserving winner. My apologies to you. I must have be asleep at the clicker when this gem whooshed by. Can I change my vote now?  :)', '2003-04-08 09:08:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(258499, 16688, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Doug...<br/> <br/>I like the color and concept on this photo quite a bit.  It''s compositionally strong and I do see the callenge interpretation here quite easily.<br/> <br/>Simply put, I believe the focus should have been on the window itself.  it appears that your camera focused on the outside environment rather than the window, and that lack of front focus seems to fail this photograph.  I believe that most of the comments you received on this issue are on target.  I''m not sure if your camera will do manual focus, but that can be helpful in a situation like this sometimes :)  <br/> <br/>Keep up the great work :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Doug... I like the color and concept on this photo quite a bit.  It''s compositionally strong and I do see the callenge interpretation here quite easily. Simply put, I believe the focus should have been on the window itself.  it appears that your camera focused on the outside environment rather than the window, and that lack of front focus seems to fail this photograph.  I believe that most of the comments you received on this issue are on target.  I''m not sure if your camera will do manual focus, but that can be helpful in a situation like this sometimes :)   Keep up the great work :) John Setzler', '2003-04-08 10:39:31.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(258500, 16176, 5514, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous Image!! This image definitely needs to be marketed!! Great Job!!</td>', 'Gorgeous Image!! This image definitely needs to be marketed!! Great Job!!', '2003-04-08 10:40:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(258577, 16075, 7082, '<td valign="top">Thanks everybody.<br/>This image is the inside of a crystal wine glass with red wine inside.  The blue comes from linen cloth underneath the glass.  Thanks for the heads up on lighting and focus I will work on it.<br/> <br/>dab<br/><a href="//www.spacetaker.org" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.spacetaker.org</a></td>', 'Thanks everybody.This image is the inside of a crystal wine glass with red wine inside.  The blue comes from linen cloth underneath the glass.  Thanks for the heads up on lighting and focus I will work on it. dab//www.spacetaker.org', '2003-04-08 11:22:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(258675, 16645, 3087, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/> <br/><b>Initial thoughts</b> <br/>Interesting content  nice silhouettes  a bit dark.	<br/> <br/><b>Composition/ Content</b> <br/>I like the unusual composition  centred on one axis but not on the other. I also like the natural element of the symmetry  the symmetry is in the two birds doing the same thing on either side of the feeding platform  but in terms of actual shapes  they are in different positions. I find that interesting. I prefer the bird on the right which I find more appealing in silhouette form.<br/> <br/><b>Background</b> <br/>Seems very dark  I think a lighter blue would allow better display of the silhouettes.<br/> <br/><b>Camera Work - Technical</b> <br/>I like the motion captured in the wings.<br/> <br/><b>Fits The Challenge</b> <br/>I believe so, yes.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion On The Photo</b> <br/>Interesting, intriguing but not wholly appealing because of the darkness. Not quite enough to really pull me back for repeat viewings.<br/></td>', 'Critique Club   Initial thoughts Interesting content  nice silhouettes  a bit dark.	 Composition/ Content I like the unusual composition  centred on one axis but not on the other. I also like the natural element of the symmetry  the symmetry is in the two birds doing the same thing on either side of the feeding platform  but in terms of actual shapes  they are in different positions. I find that interesting. I prefer the bird on the right which I find more appealing in silhouette form. Background Seems very dark  I think a lighter blue would allow better display of the silhouettes. Camera Work - Technical I like the motion captured in the wings. Fits The Challenge I believe so, yes. My Opinion On The Photo Interesting, intriguing but not wholly appealing because of the darkness. Not quite enough to really pull me back for repeat viewings.', '2003-04-08 12:16:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(258708, 16767, 656, '<td valign="top">CC: Wow - great initial impact.  The frame is full, the pattern covers almost the entire shot, and the symmetry is obvious.  A very good shot for this challenge.<br/> <br/>The composition is good - although it feels a bit amputated at the top, as if you couldn''t decide whether to show all of the tips of the frond, or show none of the tips.  I think I''d have prefered to see one extreme or the either - either no blue sky/ background at all, or all of the tips visible.  The side lighting has worked well to show the depth of the leaf, although some of the highlights on the tops seem to be slightly blown out.  This sort of harsh sidelight is hard to expose for well.  All in all a good entry, but I personally think a tighter crop would have been more decisive.</td>', 'CC: Wow - great initial impact.  The frame is full, the pattern covers almost the entire shot, and the symmetry is obvious.  A very good shot for this challenge. The composition is good - although it feels a bit amputated at the top, as if you couldn''t decide whether to show all of the tips of the frond, or show none of the tips.  I think I''d have prefered to see one extreme or the either - either no blue sky/ background at all, or all of the tips visible.  The side lighting has worked well to show the depth of the leaf, although some of the highlights on the tops seem to be slightly blown out.  This sort of harsh sidelight is hard to expose for well.  All in all a good entry, but I personally think a tighter crop would have been more decisive.', '2003-04-08 12:42:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(258713, 16567, 656, '<td valign="top">Shows good symmetry, and the lighting is very soft and even, highlighting the veins/ features of the skin.  I personally like these sorts of shots with a touch more contrast but that is fairly subjective.  <br/> <br/>The painted toes vs the non-painted finger nails disturbs me for some reason and the left toes seem like they could do with some touch-up in the paint department - might just be highlights.  A good attempt.</td>', 'Shows good symmetry, and the lighting is very soft and even, highlighting the veins/ features of the skin.  I personally like these sorts of shots with a touch more contrast but that is fairly subjective.   The painted toes vs the non-painted finger nails disturbs me for some reason and the left toes seem like they could do with some touch-up in the paint department - might just be highlights.  A good attempt.', '2003-04-08 12:46:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(258717, 16638, 6900, '<td valign="top">Jason - push "OK" then "mode menu" then push right arrow to get into "camera" settings then scroll to the bottom or push the up arrow once.  push the right arrow on "2 in 1" - now take your first half of the pic, take the second - now preview in-camera what happened. :)<br/> <br/>Joebar - my Olympus cam can take two shots and interlace them - that''s how I took this shot as "all in camera" photog stuff is legal.<br/> <br/>Gudsteinn - thank you.  I''ve gotten over the points and now I want good photos.</td>', 'Jason - push "OK" then "mode menu" then push right arrow to get into "camera" settings then scroll to the bottom or push the up arrow once.  push the right arrow on "2 in 1" - now take your first half of the pic, take the second - now preview in-camera what happened. :) Joebar - my Olympus cam can take two shots and interlace them - that''s how I took this shot as "all in camera" photog stuff is legal. Gudsteinn - thank you.  I''ve gotten over the points and now I want good photos.', '2003-04-08 12:59:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(258750, 16630, 3290, '<td valign="top">Really nice. Very striking picture and a neat trick.</td>', 'Really nice. Very striking picture and a neat trick.', '2003-04-08 13:48:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(259265, 16013, 7160, '<td valign="top">.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-10-04 19:12:17.</i></td>', '.', '2003-04-08 17:07:31.000000', '2005-10-04 20:12:17.000000', 0),
(259351, 16157, 368, '<td valign="top">hi there from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>I didnt vote this past week but this image is a very nice shot of symmetry ... <br/> <br/>the tones, angle and color capture really does show the depth of field in this photo ... personal opinion i would have liked to see this a little sharper but it''s a good shot none the less<br/> <br/>composition of this photo is also very appealing to the eye .. kinda looks like the cube is floating at first but then you see the shadow at the bottom - very nice effect<br/> <br/>this object shows symmetry in almost a 3way view ... if only you coulda suspended some of the balls up top - haha<br/> <br/>great job .. keep it up ... Ayme</td>', 'hi there from the Critique Club I didnt vote this past week but this image is a very nice shot of symmetry ...  the tones, angle and color capture really does show the depth of field in this photo ... personal opinion i would have liked to see this a little sharper but it''s a good shot none the less composition of this photo is also very appealing to the eye .. kinda looks like the cube is floating at first but then you see the shadow at the bottom - very nice effect this object shows symmetry in almost a 3way view ... if only you coulda suspended some of the balls up top - haha great job .. keep it up ... Ayme', '2003-04-08 18:07:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(259356, 16176, 5592, '<td valign="top">I love these colored night light shots. Yours was one of the best i have seen. I would love to have a copy of the original image.<br/>Well done!</td>', 'I love these colored night light shots. Yours was one of the best i have seen. I would love to have a copy of the original image.Well done!', '2003-04-08 18:09:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(259526, 16634, 327, '<td valign="top"><b>CC</b>  Greetings stephan <br/> <br/>Fits The Challenge-Yes <br/>Composition- Lovely <br/>Background- Fantastic *<b>mesmerizing</b>*<br/>My Opinion- Some shots just get shoved aside, looked at too quickly or not seen for their beauty. Also there are times when others shine and they get higher scores. Nuttin'' ya can do. This was a wonderful photo. Nothing wrong with it. Great colors, light. Stunning work. Keep your chin up and keep shooting.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-04-08 19:23:03.</i></td>', 'CC  Greetings stephan  Fits The Challenge-Yes Composition- Lovely Background- Fantastic *mesmerizing*My Opinion- Some shots just get shoved aside, looked at too quickly or not seen for their beauty. Also there are times when others shine and they get higher scores. Nuttin'' ya can do. This was a wonderful photo. Nothing wrong with it. Great colors, light. Stunning work. Keep your chin up and keep shooting.', '2003-04-08 20:22:35.000000', '2003-04-08 20:23:03.000000', 0),
(259533, 16494, 327, '<td valign="top"><b>CC</b>  Hello sylandrix, happy Tuesday.<br/> <br/>Fits The Challenge-Yes -nice symmetry.<br/>Composition- Nice <br/>Background- Nice, but a bit boring IMHO. <br/>My Opinion- Like a few below I see this as _too_ bright. That would be my thinking for a different colored background. Still I do understand why you chose the white although it doesn''t seem to pop! Because this is so centered and shot head on it appears to just sit there. Here I think a mirror would of worked well. Something to jazz it up a bit. Good luck in the next challege.<br/> <br/></td>', 'CC  Hello sylandrix, happy Tuesday. Fits The Challenge-Yes -nice symmetry.Composition- Nice Background- Nice, but a bit boring IMHO. My Opinion- Like a few below I see this as _too_ bright. That would be my thinking for a different colored background. Still I do understand why you chose the white although it doesn''t seem to pop! Because this is so centered and shot head on it appears to just sit there. Here I think a mirror would of worked well. Something to jazz it up a bit. Good luck in the next challege. ', '2003-04-08 20:31:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(259590, 16625, 1647, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Composition: The composition of this image is very good.  The spacing around the shoes works well.  I really like the mirror style effect you created.<br/> <br/>Technical Quality: Technically the shot is ok, but could probably be improved slightly.  The lighting is a little harsh, but nothing too serious.  The focus looks a bit blurry - did you try sharpening the image to define some of the edges.<br/> <br/>Meeting the Challenge: I really like your approach to the challenge.  Your decision to make the shoes different was very wise - otherwise it would look like a shoe on a mirror (making for a rather boring photo).  The shoelace was a good decision, the tab at the back probably wasn''t necessary, but certainly isn''t a problem.<br/> <br/>Creativity: Again, a reflected shoe is a pretty boring subject.  But a pretend reflection with an obvious difference was very smart.  It''s the kind of photo that if hung on a wall would have people look at it thinking "why photo that" until they realised the humour in it.<br/> <br/>Border: The border is nice and subtle.  Good job.<br/> <br/>Overall: I really like the concept in this photo.  It isn''t technically perfect, with the focus being my main distraction.  Good work on a very amusing photo.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Critique Club Composition: The composition of this image is very good.  The spacing around the shoes works well.  I really like the mirror style effect you created. Technical Quality: Technically the shot is ok, but could probably be improved slightly.  The lighting is a little harsh, but nothing too serious.  The focus looks a bit blurry - did you try sharpening the image to define some of the edges. Meeting the Challenge: I really like your approach to the challenge.  Your decision to make the shoes different was very wise - otherwise it would look like a shoe on a mirror (making for a rather boring photo).  The shoelace was a good decision, the tab at the back probably wasn''t necessary, but certainly isn''t a problem. Creativity: Again, a reflected shoe is a pretty boring subject.  But a pretend reflection with an obvious difference was very smart.  It''s the kind of photo that if hung on a wall would have people look at it thinking "why photo that" until they realised the humour in it. Border: The border is nice and subtle.  Good job. Overall: I really like the concept in this photo.  It isn''t technically perfect, with the focus being my main distraction.  Good work on a very amusing photo. ', '2003-04-08 21:10:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(259656, 16516, 6536, '<td valign="top">Great black &amp; white shot. Nice composition &amp; cropping. Good job.</td>', 'Great black & white shot. Nice composition & cropping. Good job.', '2003-04-08 22:15:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(259708, 16630, 368, '<td valign="top">hey there from the Critique Club ..<br/>from the first time i saw this photo it amazed me ... and at first i didnt think anything of the placement of the reflections ... the composition is great - my eyes are led through the photo to see all there is to see and i love the idea of flipping it over ... i''ll definitly have to try that some time ... the light and tones are evenly spread out and the detail in the sihloette (SP?) of the trees is amazing ... I did not get a chance to vote this past week but this much deserves to be in the top 3 spot! great job!</td>', 'hey there from the Critique Club ..from the first time i saw this photo it amazed me ... and at first i didnt think anything of the placement of the reflections ... the composition is great - my eyes are led through the photo to see all there is to see and i love the idea of flipping it over ... i''ll definitly have to try that some time ... the light and tones are evenly spread out and the detail in the sihloette (SP?) of the trees is amazing ... I did not get a chance to vote this past week but this much deserves to be in the top 3 spot! great job!', '2003-04-08 22:50:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(259719, 16176, 327, '<td valign="top"><b>CC  Hi Gordon</b> <br/> <br/>Fits The Challenge-OH yeah! <br/>Composition-Fantastic <br/>Background-Night  <br/>My Opinion-This is just perfectly perfect. Your work is ''clean''..all of your shots are. I can almost recognize your work during a challenge. The colors on the black water are spectacular and please the eye. Everything is neat, clean, sharp, and crisp. Love it!!<br/></td>', 'CC  Hi Gordon  Fits The Challenge-OH yeah! Composition-Fantastic Background-Night  My Opinion-This is just perfectly perfect. Your work is ''clean''..all of your shots are. I can almost recognize your work during a challenge. The colors on the black water are spectacular and please the eye. Everything is neat, clean, sharp, and crisp. Love it!!', '2003-04-08 22:58:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(259737, 16558, 368, '<td valign="top">hey there from the critique club!<br/> <br/>this is a great image! i love the combination of symmetry that is used -first focal point would of course be from the center and each sides are the same and the composition also add a nice demension to the image .. great job! I would have to agree with inspzil that a deeper blue sky could definitly add a little more impact ... maybe play around with the saturation levels and see what happens ... regardless it''s still an awesome shot!</td>', 'hey there from the critique club! this is a great image! i love the combination of symmetry that is used -first focal point would of course be from the center and each sides are the same and the composition also add a nice demension to the image .. great job! I would have to agree with inspzil that a deeper blue sky could definitly add a little more impact ... maybe play around with the saturation levels and see what happens ... regardless it''s still an awesome shot!', '2003-04-08 23:05:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(259986, 16389, 368, '<td valign="top">hey there from the Critique Club - hehe<br/> <br/>this image is excellent .. the clarity and detail in the clear figures is amazing .. i do like the shallow DOF and the play in with the chessboard .. the placement of everything certainly portrays symmetry and the off balance in the background sets the complete composition off nicely ... I also do like the blue tones it gives it a warmer feeling - maybe even a more artsy feel to the photograph than if the shot was done in black and white  ... my only thing is that the King looks like its slightly leaning to the right ... maybe it''s just an illusion or the piece itself ... either way ...  great job .. Ayme</td>', 'hey there from the Critique Club - hehe this image is excellent .. the clarity and detail in the clear figures is amazing .. i do like the shallow DOF and the play in with the chessboard .. the placement of everything certainly portrays symmetry and the off balance in the background sets the complete composition off nicely ... I also do like the blue tones it gives it a warmer feeling - maybe even a more artsy feel to the photograph than if the shot was done in black and white  ... my only thing is that the King looks like its slightly leaning to the right ... maybe it''s just an illusion or the piece itself ... either way ...  great job .. Ayme', '2003-04-09 01:20:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(259991, 16631, 368, '<td valign="top">hi there from the critique club ...<br/> <br/>first off i have to say .. i love shoe shots! hehe<br/>this image is great in detail with the laces and loop holes of the boot ... with the intertwining of the laces up the boot it certainly shows symmetry ... i love the tones in the black and white and the texture that you have captured with this photo - the composition is just right... great job<br/> <br/>Ayme</td>', 'hi there from the critique club ... first off i have to say .. i love shoe shots! hehethis image is great in detail with the laces and loop holes of the boot ... with the intertwining of the laces up the boot it certainly shows symmetry ... i love the tones in the black and white and the texture that you have captured with this photo - the composition is just right... great job Ayme', '2003-04-09 01:23:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(260015, 16336, 1647, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Composition: Composition wise you have done very well.  The cropping on all sides is nicely balanced and the photo has a pleasing aspect ratio.  I like the way that the background fades darker as well.  Locking the clips together shows the symmetry well.<br/> <br/>Technical Quality: The focus and depth of field is very good.  The shadows are well done (overhead lighting worked very well).  The blown out highlights at the top edges are a shame, but also remind the viewer that the clips are glossy and reflective - overall they are probably better included than removed.  The background is very well done.<br/> <br/>Meeting the Challenge: You have met the symmetry challenge whilst still providing an interesting image.  They have symmetry, without being "absolutely" symmetrical - which is nice.<br/> <br/>Creativity: I like the difference in colour between the clips, despite their similarity.  Locking them together was very good.<br/> <br/>Border: The simple black border is nice.  Simple is almost always nice when it comes to borders.<br/> <br/>Overall: I like this photo - you''ve done well to make a basic object look appealing.  I''m surprised this image didn''t rate slightly higher actually.  Well done.<br/></td>', 'Critique Club Composition: Composition wise you have done very well.  The cropping on all sides is nicely balanced and the photo has a pleasing aspect ratio.  I like the way that the background fades darker as well.  Locking the clips together shows the symmetry well. Technical Quality: The focus and depth of field is very good.  The shadows are well done (overhead lighting worked very well).  The blown out highlights at the top edges are a shame, but also remind the viewer that the clips are glossy and reflective - overall they are probably better included than removed.  The background is very well done. Meeting the Challenge: You have met the symmetry challenge whilst still providing an interesting image.  They have symmetry, without being "absolutely" symmetrical - which is nice. Creativity: I like the difference in colour between the clips, despite their similarity.  Locking them together was very good. Border: The simple black border is nice.  Simple is almost always nice when it comes to borders. Overall: I like this photo - you''ve done well to make a basic object look appealing.  I''m surprised this image didn''t rate slightly higher actually.  Well done.', '2003-04-09 02:07:07.000000', NULL, 0),
